We run the internal IT helpdesk for a 300-person company. Tickets come in by mail and phone, a dispatcher assigns them to an agent in the right team, agents add notes and resolve. We need to see overdue tickets at a glance and never lose a ticket in waiting. Flows: open a new ticket (reporter details, priority, category, optionally the affected asset), assign or reassign a ticket to an active agent, add a note to a ticket. Public page: employees without helpdesk access should be able to submit a support request – title, description, their contact details. Every request arrives as New with priority Medium; requesters never see status, priority, agents or internal notes